Subject: [PATCH 06947/11362] [outer-loop] Task 9: InertClickSigPruner
 dead-signature click pruning (REQ-ARC-FCP-5595)

Built InertClickSigPruner (python/carnot/agentic/arc_inert_click_pruner.py),
extending Reki's dead-signature click-pruning idea via HazardMovePruner's
trust+specificity gating discipline instead of Reki's own greedy K=2
threshold (flagged over-aggressive by the perception-grounding audit). Per
structural signature (color, size, is_rect, twin_count) -- computed via a
new click_signature() helper and a new blob_at_click() free function
(promoted from ColorBlobSaliencePrior's private _blob_for_click, purely
additive) -- the pruner tracks (obs, inert, leveled) counts and prunes only
once min_observations=4 (not K=2) AND min_specificity=0.9 (not zero-
tolerance) both clear, with any ever-leveled signature permanently sacred.
Twin blobs sharing a signature transfer evidence to each other.

Implements the identical should_prune/observe protocol as HazardMovePruner
and RelationalMaskMovePruner, so it composes through the existing
CompositeMovePruner and is live-path-reachable via OfflineSolver's
move_pruner= param with no new wiring. A separate rank_candidates method
matches StepwiseExplorer._candidates's filter-protocol shape but is
deliberately not yet wired into that live composition chain -- a distinct,
separately-scoped step (mirrors the still-open color-blob live-wiring
decision, task #97).

7 unit tests pass on synthetic grids. The offline-sim prototype fed real
transitions from a real E3AgentPolicy exploration of m0r0 (confirmed
click-heavy: 21/22 transitions were clicks): 37 transitions, 32 clicks, 12
distinct signatures tracked, 0 confidently inert at this budget -- an
honest null (average <3 observations per signature, below the evidence
floor for most; the gate is designed to fail closed under sparse evidence).
inference_substrate was corrected mid-task from an initial live_llm_inference
guess to offline_arcade_live_agent_runtime_self_discovery_no_llm after
adversarial_verify.py correctly flagged DURATION_TOO_SHORT (19.3s measured
vs the 60s live-inference floor) -- the proposer is wired but never actually
invoked during pure exploration.

